{
  "_comment": [
    "The atriumd service definition: what peinit starts, and how.",
    "",
    "Identity is LocalService for now: this slice binds 8080, which is an",
    "unreserved port and so anyone's once port-reservations.reg applies, and",
    "does nothing else. It will move to SYSTEM when it starts originating",
    "logons (logon.sock admits SYSTEM alone, and installing another",
    "principal's token needs SeTcbPrivilege) -- recorded here so that move is",
    "a known step rather than a surprise.",
    "",
    "Readiness is Notify (0): atriumd sends READY=1 once its listener is",
    "bound.",
    "",
    "RestartPolicy is Always (2): a machine whose session host is down has",
    "no way for its users to reach it, and a restart costs nothing yet.",
    "",
    "Shipped by the atriumd package into /usr/share/regim/; inert until an",
    "image names it in [registry] autoapply."
  ],
  "keys": [
    { "path": "Machine\\System" },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Services" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Services\\atriumd",
      "values": [
        { "name": "ImagePath", "type": "sz", "data": "/usr/sbin/atriumd" },
        { "name": "Triggers", "type": "multi", "data": ["boot"] },
        { "name": "Identity", "type": "sz", "data": "LocalService" },
        { "name": "Readiness", "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "RestartPolicy", "type": "dword", "data": 2 },
        { "name": "ErrorControl", "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "DisplayName", "type": "sz", "data": "Atrium web session host" },
        { "name": "Description", "type": "sz", "data": "The Peios web UI: serves the browser-delivered session on port 8080" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
